  "rules": "complexity: ordinal median (trivial<low<medium<high<expert) of the non-null votes once sorted: an odd count takes the middle vote, an even count the mean of the two middle tier indices (n/2-1 and n/2) rounded down (low+high -> medium, low+medium -> low; docs/34 §0.3); null when the null votes are strictly more than half (7 of 12 is undecidable, 6 of 12 is not). truth_all: the main judges' votes on the 4 language versions of the base key (3 judges = 12 votes), repeated on each version; truth_lang: their votes on the id. task, needs_tools: majority of the non-null votes, a tie going to the value voted first in priority order (--main order, then the ids of the base key in prompts file order). *_nogemma: the same without the main judges whose model contains 'gemma'. undecidable: truth_all.complexity is null. spread: max - min tier index over the main judges' non-null votes on the id. lang_disagreement: truth_lang.complexity and truth_all.complexity both non-null and different. An abstention (a judge's row with `abstained`: no answer) is a null vote on every field: out of every median, majority and spread, counted as a null toward undecidable."
}
